@startuml
title sol2uml PNG export on Ubuntu 23.10+ with Puppeteer's bundled Chrome
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  ParticipantBorderColor #B54A4A
}
participant sol2uml
participant Puppeteer
participant "Chrome\n(<U+007E>/.cache/puppeteer)" as C
participant "Kernel + AppArmor" as K
sol2uml -> sol2uml : parse Solidity, layout SVG (viz.js)
sol2uml -> Puppeteer : convert SVG to PNG
Puppeteer -> C : launch headless
C -> K : create user namespace
K --> C : allowed, moved to unprivileged_userns
C -> K : use CAP_SYS_ADMIN in namespace
K --> C : DENIED (sys_admin)
C --> Puppeteer : FATAL No usable sandbox!
Puppeteer --> sol2uml : Failed to launch the browser process
note over sol2uml : Failed to convert PNG file\n(-f dot + Graphviz, -f svg, or a profiled\nChrome via PUPPETEER_EXECUTABLE_PATH avoid it)
@enduml
